## 7. The prep table

Alongside the evidence bank, build a one-page navigation table so you can find the right answer within seconds during the discussion. This is the single most useful document to have open on the day.

| Theme | KSBs | Evidence title | One-line hook | Where it is |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| B | S4, S9, K24 | Payments API rebuild | Designed, coded, and tested the integration layer with threat modelling and retry logic | Portfolio p.12 / bank #05 |
| C | S20, S21 | Mid-sprint compliance pivot | Re-planned the sprint, revised recommendations, influenced the team's approach | Portfolio p.18 / bank #09 |

Fill in one row per prepared answer. Then build the reverse of it: one row per submitted portfolio item, listing the workplace stories that extend it. Since the assessor's questions start from the portfolio, the reverse index is the one you'll reach for first. Print both, or keep them on a second screen next to the portfolio.

