## 9. On the day

Test your kit and software ahead of time, and have your photo ID ready. Keep water, pen and paper, your prep table, and your portfolio (open on screen or printed) beside you. When a question lands: replay part of it back to anchor yourself, name the portfolio project you'll use, state your role, and work through your STARE answer in the first person. It's fine to pause and check your notes, and it's fine to ask the assessor whether they'd like more detail. Re-read the whole portfolio the day before so it's fresh, and do a vocal warm-up if you're not used to speaking at length.

One last reminder, borrowed from an apprentice who's been through it: the portfolio is not directly assessed; it exists to help you pass the professional discussion. Build it for you.
